# minimum required Qore version
%requires qore >= 2.0
%modern

%requires(reexport) DataProvider
%requires(reexport) WSDL
%requires(reexport) SoapClient

module SoapDataProvider {
    version = "2.0";
    desc = "user module providing a data provider API for SOAP messaging";
    author = "David Nichols <david@qore.org>";
    url = "http://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
    init = sub () {
        # register the data provider factory
        DataProvider::registerFactory(new SoapDataProviderFactory());

        # register the data provider application
        DataProviderActionCatalog::registerApp(<DataProviderAppInfo>{
            "name": SoapDataProvider::AppName,
            "presentation_source_locale": "en",
            "display_name": "SOAP Server",
            "short_desc": "SOAP server for SOAP API calls",
            "desc": "Provides integration with **SOAP** web services for making API calls.\n\n"
                "Use this app when you need to:\n"
                "- Call SOAP operations defined in a WSDL\n"
                "- Integrate with legacy SOAP-based APIs\n\n"
                "Supports SOAP 1.1 and 1.2 with configurable headers and XML options.",
            "groups": (DataProvider::AppGroup::ApiIntegration,),
            "scheme": "soap",
            "logo": SoapLogoLight,
            "logo_file_name": "generic-soap-logo.svg",
            "logo_mime_type": MimeTypeSvg,
        });

        # register all supported actions
        DataProviderActionCatalog::registerAction(<DataProviderActionInfo>{
            "app": SoapDataProvider::AppName,
            "path": "/{api}",
            "action": "call-soap-api",
            "display_name": "Call SOAP API",
            "short_desc": "Call a SOAP API",
            "desc": "Call a SOAP API operation defined in the WSDL.\n\n"
                "The operation to call is selected via the `api` path variable. "
                "Optional SOAP and HTTP headers can be provided, along with XML generation "
                "options and SOAP binding selection.",
            "action_code": DPAT_API,
            "output_type": AbstractDataProviderTypeMap."auto",
            "path_vars": {
                "api": <DataProviderPathVarInfo>{
                    "display_name": "API",
                    "short_desc": "The SOAP operation to call",
                    "desc": "The SOAP operation to call",
                },
            },
        });
    };
}

/** @mainpage SoapDataProvider Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section soapdataproviderintro Introduction to the SoapDataProvider Module

    The %SoapDataProvider module provides a @ref dataproviderintro "data provider" API for SOAP messaging.  The
    @ref SoapDataProvider::SoapDataProvider "SoapDataProvider" class allows for introspecting a SOAP schema, while the
    @ref SoapDataProvider::SoapRequestDataProvider "SoapRequestDataProvider" class
    supports the @ref dataproviderintro "data provider" request-reply API for communication with SOAP servers.

    Each operation is a child provider named after the operation, for example \c getInfo.
    The child is a @ref SoapDataProvider::SoapRequestDataProvider "SoapRequestDataProvider" object that exposes
    both the request and response types and can send a request to the server.

    @par Example
    Inspect the request and response definitions before calling a customer information operation:
    @code{.qore}
    SoapDataProvider provider({"schema_location": "file:///srv/schemas/customer.wsdl"});
    AbstractDataProvider operation = provider.getChildProviderEx("getInfo");
    *AbstractDataProviderType request_type = operation.getRequestType();
    *AbstractDataProviderType response_type = operation.getResponseType();
    @endcode

    The following classes are provided by this module:
    - @ref SoapDataProvider::SoapDataProvider "SoapDataProvider"
    - @ref SoapDataProvider::SoapDataProviderBase "SoapDataProviderBase"
    - @ref SoapDataProvider::SoapDataProviderFactory "SoapDataProviderFactory"
    - @ref SoapDataProvider::SoapRequestDataProvider "SoapRequestDataProvider"

    An explicit native SOAP value can separate overlapping Body and Header parts:
    @code{.qore}
    operation.doRequest({"^body^": {"order": order, "token": "body-token"},
        "^headers^": {"OrderMessage": {"token": "header-token"}}});
    @endcode
    Both maps are required. The body uses the abstract message's schema validation; headers are validated
    against the selected SOAP binding before transmission. Do not also supply a nonempty soap_header option.
    getRequestTypeWithData() describes this representation when supplied; static request/response type metadata
    continues to describe the abstract message's part map for ordinary SOAP bindings.

    SOAP MIME bindings use WSDL::WsdlSoapMimeDataType for concrete request/response metadata and validation.
    Type-based attachments accept raw media bytes independently of the abstract XSD type. Element-based
    attachments validate their schema XML. Explicit values add a required ^attachments^ map alongside
    ^body^ and ^headers^. The configured client's binding, or its default service port, selects this contract.
    @code{.qore}
    operation.doRequest({"^body^": {"invoice": original}, "^headers^": {},
        "^attachments^": {"invoice": signed_copy}});
    @endcode
    Binding-aware examples use separate maps for overlapping part identities; media alternatives choose a
    declared concrete type. A wildcard-only media declaration requires a supplied concrete example.

    @section soapdataprovider_relnotes Release Notes

    @subsection soapdataprovider_v2_0 SoapDataProvider v2.0
    - HTTP multipart providers retain entity trees, validate their selected binding and expose recursive MIME call options
    - SOAP MIME request and response types follow the selected binding, preserve raw attachment data and
      validate complete body/header/attachment placement before transmission, including saved provider types
    - accept explicit ^body^ and ^headers^ maps for independent values in overlapping SOAP parts,
      retaining schema validation before transmission
    - added support for the data provider action catalog API
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4808">issue 4808</a>)

    @subsection soapdataprovider_v1_1 SoapDataProvider v1.1
    - fixed a bug where data providers could return local names as paths with \c "/" characters in them, breaking
      some clients traversing the data provider hierarchy
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4555">issue 4555</a>)

    @subsection soapdataprovider_v1_0 SoapDataProvider v1.0
    - initial release of the module
*/

#! contains all public definitions in the SoapDataProvider module
public namespace SoapDataProvider {
}

namespace Priv {
    const SoapLogoLight = File::readTextFile(get_script_dir() + "/generic-soap-logo.svg");
    const SoapLogoDark = File::readTextFile(get_script_dir() + "/generic-soap-logo-dark.svg");
}
